          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              There is
              %em no
              condition on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
              %em not
              required to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-monomorphisms"} n-monomorphisms
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-epimorphisms"} n-epimorphisms
              for any
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              On the other hand, while they are also not explicitly required to have a presentation by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+for+spectra"} model structures for spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              or by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            %p
              This means that we may think of a filtration on a spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
              as equivalently being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower+of+fibrations"} tower of fibrations
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The following remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnrolledExactCoupleOfAFiltrationOnASpectrum"}
            unravels the structure encoded in a filtration on a spectrum, and motivates the concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+couples"} exact couples
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequences"} spectral sequences
            from these.
